NekoJump (猫ジャンプ)
=====================
A silly `cd` command that learns you :3

Installation
============
```
# mkdir -p /usr/share/zsh/plugins/nekojump
# cp nekojump.plugin.zsh /usr/share/zsh/plugins/nekojump/
```

and make sure to `source` it somewhere in your shell startup scripts

```
source /usr/share/zsh/plugins/nekojump/nekojump.plugin.zsh
```

Why `NekoJump`?
===============

Because cats don’t search — they *know* where to go.
Highest shelf, warmest spot, most-used directory… effortless.

`NekoJump` learns your habits and jumps there instantly.


AI chose this name because my original name was so good that I had to change it
so you wouldn't immediately fall in love with me.



Why use this over `zoxide` or `autojump`?
=========================================

Because it’s cuter :3

Also:

* no magic, just a simple script
* uses only standard Unix utilities
* easy to read, tweak, debug, and eat.
* does exactly what you expect — nothing more


Usage
=====
NekoJump provides several functions to manipulate and read the `$NEKOJUMP_DATABASE`:

**Core Commands:**
* `nekojump <query>` - Jump to a directory by name or path (searches database for best match)
* `nekojumpi [query]` - Interactive directory selection with fzf and live preview
* `nekojumpback` - Go back to the previous directory
* `nekojumpd [path]` - Remove a directory from the database (default: current directory)

**Utilities & Information:**
* `nekojumpclean` - Clean up non-existent directories from the database
* `nekojumptop [count]` - Show your most-visited directories (default: top 10)
* `nekojumprecent [count]` - Show recently visited directories with timestamps (default: 10)
* `nekojumpfreq <directory>` - Show frequency score for a specific directory
* `nekojumpstats` - Display database statistics (total dirs, location, size)

**Quick Aliases:**
```
alias z='nekojump'           # Jump to directory
alias zi='nekojumpi'         # Interactive jump with preview
alias zd='nekojumpd'         # Delete from database
alias zb='nekojumpback'      # Go to previous directory (pounce back!)
alias zcl='nekojumpclean'    # Clean dead entries
alias ztop='nekojumptop'     # Show top directories
alias zrecent='nekojumprecent' # Show recent directories
alias zfreq='nekojumpfreq'   # Check frequency of a directory
alias zstats='nekojumpstats' # Show database info
```

